<%# One link of the sidebar, as a <wa-button>. The code renders it at the top level and in the panel
    of a group, and that is the reason for a partial.
    ⚠️ `data-drawer="close"` is what closes the drawer on a mobile screen after a tap. Without it,
    the drawer stays open over the page that the link opened. It is on the host element, and the
    document handler of <wa-drawer> and its handler in the drawer both look there: a click in a
    shadow root goes to the host before either handler sees it. %>
<% current = admin_nav_current?(item[:path]) %>
<li>
  <%# `appearance` gives the active state: filled for the current page, and plain for each other
      page. Those are the values of Web Awesome, and not a background that a person selects.
      `aria-current` stays for the meaning, but ⚠️ a screen reader does NOT read it: <wa-button>
      renders its own <a> in a shadow root and sends no ARIA of the host to it. Thus the current
      item also has a visually-hidden marker in its label, as the new-tab hint does. %>
  <%= tag.wa_button class: "admin-nav__link",
                    href: item[:path],
                    appearance: current ? "filled" : "plain",
                    target: (item[:external] ? "_blank" : nil),
                    rel: (item[:external] ? "noopener" : nil),
                    data: { drawer: "close" },
                    aria: { current: current ? "page" : nil } do %>
    <%= slotted_icon_svg(*item[:icon]) %>
    <%= item[:label] %>
    <% if current %>
      <span class="wa-visually-hidden">, current page</span>
    <% end %>
    <% if item[:badge] %>
      <%# ⚠️ This is in a span. A <wa-badge> in a slot of a <wa-button> becomes a small dot at a
          corner, and on a nav button of the full width, that dot goes outside the button. %>
      <span slot="end">
        <wa-badge pill>
          <%= item[:badge] %>
          <span class="wa-visually-hidden">waiting</span>
        </wa-badge>
      </span>
    <% end %>
    <% if item[:external] %>
      <span slot="end" class="admin-nav__hint wa-caption-s"><%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "arrow-up-right-from-square") %></span>
      <span class="wa-visually-hidden">(opens in a new tab)</span>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</li>
